i:"__root__␀",u:1791288462163,s:"success",ssr:!0},$R[12]={i:"␀case-studies␀case-studies",u:1791288462163,s:"success",ssr:!0},$R[13]={i:"␀case-studies␀$slug␀case-studies␀manufacturer-sales-distribution-audit",u:1791288462163,s:"success",l:$R[14]={kind:"study",study:$R[15]={slug:"manufacturer-sales-distribution-audit",name:"Unlocking Sales Growth for a Mid-Sized Manufacturing Business",industry:"Manufacturing • Industrial Products",engagement:"Business Audit • Sales & Distribution Strategy",client:"Confidential",challenge:"A mid-sized manufacturing business with established operations and documented processes was struggling to grow its top line. The founder recognised something was off — but couldn't pinpoint where.",keyQuestion:"Why is a well-run business not growing at the pace it should?",approachLead:"SBC conducted a 45-Minute Complementary Business Audit covering people, process, systems, and strategy. The audit included the founder and HR leadership.",approachNarrative:$R[16]=["What emerged quickly: internal operations were largely in order. SOPs existed. Accountability structures were functional. The business was not broken inside.","The bottleneck was outside — in the market."],approachBullets:$R[17]=["Sales structure and coverage","Dealer and distributor network depth and activity","Channel engagement and incentive design","Market penetration vs. potential","Founder dependency on key accounts"],findingsHeading:"What We Found",findings:$R[18]=["Dealer and distributor network existed but was underactivated — relationships were passive, not managed","No structured channel engagement or performance tracking","Sales effort was reactive — responding to inbound rather than driving outbound","Key account relationships were concentrated at the founder level with no team coverage beneath"],strategicDirectionLead:"The recommended direction was built around:",flow:$R[19]=["Active Channel Management","Distributor Performance Framework","Sales Team Activation","Account Coverage Mapping","Pipeline Visibility"],recommendations:$R[20]=["Audit the existing dealer and distributor network — identify who is active, who is dormant, and why","Design a channel engagement framework with defined targets, visit cadence, and incentive structure","Shift sales effort from reactive to structured — territory coverage, account mapping, and pipeline tracking","Reduce founder dependency on key relationships by building team-level account ownership","Create visibility into the sales pipeline so decisions are data-driven, not gut-driven"],outcome:"The 45-minute audit surfaced what months of internal review had not: the business did not have an operations problem. It had a sales and distribution problem — and a clear path to address it.",approachSummary:"A 45-minute business audit covering people, process, systems and strategy found that the bottleneck was not inside the business, but outside it, in the market.",badge:"45-Minute Business Audit — Sales & Distribution"},group:$R[21]={key:"business-operations",heading:"Business Operations (MSME)",label:"Business Operations (MSME)",headingLine1:"Business Operations",headingLine2:"(MSME)",practiceHref:"/msme-consulting",ctaQuestion:"Facing a similar challenge in your business?",ctaButtonText:"Book a Review",ctaButtonHref:"/msme-consulting#book",studies:$R[22]=[$R[23]={slug:"manufacturer-accountability-system",name:"Building an Accountability System for a Legacy Manufacturer",industry:"Manufacturing",engagement:"Operational Diagnostic • SOP Design • Communication Protocol • Accountability Framework • Implementation Support",client:"Confidential",challenge:"A well-established manufacturing company with decades of experience, institutional clients, and existing systems including ERP and defined KPIs — yet operational discipline remained inconsistent. The directors' observation was precise: \"Everything is in place — but people are not following the process.\"",keyQuestion:"Why was a resourced and experienced organisation unable to sustain operational discipline — and what would actually fix it?",approachLead:"SBC evaluated:",approachBullets:$R[24]=["Actual practice versus defined process across all departments","Where accountability was defined versus where it was assumed","How information travelled across the organisation","Where consequences for non-compliance were undefined","The degree to which directors were functioning as the operational system"],strategicDirectionLead:"The root cause was not people willingness. It was three interconnected gaps:",rootCauses:$R[25]=[$R[26]={title:"No written communication culture",body:"Operations ran on verbal instruction and memory with no paper trail."},$R[27]={title:"Accountability without consequence",body:"Roles and KPIs existed but non-compliance had no defined outcome."},$R[28]={title:"Founder as the system",body:"Decisions consistently escalated to the directors, leaving no self-correcting mechanism within the organisation."}],recommendations:$R[29]=["Embed written communication as a mandatory step within every process — not an optional record","Define accountability with a clear owner, checker, timeline, and consequence for every key function","Establish a communication protocol defining what gets recorded, by whom, to whom, and by when","Train department heads and key staff before compliance review begins","Deliver structured weekly reporting to directors — replacing the need to chase departments individually","Allow adequate adoption time before any SOP revision is considered"],outcome:"SBC designed and delivered a full operational accountability system across all departments — covering SOP design, accountability matrix, communication protocol, department training, implementation support, and a close-out compliance scorecard. The objective was not to add documentation — but to build the information architecture that makes accountability automatic and measurable without founder involvement.",approachSummary:"SBC traced the gap between defined process and actual practice across every department to find the real root cause of the breakdown.",badge:"Full Accountability System — Diagnostic to Implementation"},$R[15]]}},ssr:!0}],lastMatchId:"␀case-studies␀$slug␀case-studies␀manufacturer-sales-distribution-audit"})($R["tsr"]);$_TSR.e();document.currentScript.remove()</script><script type="module" async="" src="/assets/index-CccIN8c5.js"></script></body></html>